(Question 1) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(\(a\) Claim: 5n! + 2n^2 + 3n is O\(n!\).) Tj
T*
(For n >= 4, n! >= n^2 and 2n^2 + 3n <= 3n^2. Therefore,) Tj
T*
(5n! + 2n^2 + 3n <= 5n! + 3n! = 8n!.) Tj
T*
(Taking c = 8 and n0 = 4 satisfies the definition of O\(n!\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(\(b\) Claim: sqrt\(7n^2 + 2n - 8\) is Theta\(n\).) Tj
T*
(For n >= 2,) Tj
T*
(4n^2 <= 7n^2 + 2n - 8 <= 9n^2.) Tj
T*
(Taking square roots gives) Tj
T*
(2n <= sqrt\(7n^2 + 2n - 8\) <= 3n.) Tj
T*
(Thus c1 = 2, c2 = 3, and n0 = 2 satisfy the definition of Theta\(n\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(\(c\) Since d\(n\) = O\(f\(n\)\), there are constants c1 > 0 and n1 such that) Tj
T*
(0 <= d\(n\) <= c1 f\(n\) for n >= n1. Since e\(n\) = O\(g\(n\)\), there are) Tj
T*
(constants c2 > 0 and n2 such that 0 <= e\(n\) <= c2 g\(n\) for n >= n2.) Tj
T*
(For n >= max\(n1, n2\), multiplying the two inequalities gives) Tj
T*
(d\(n\)e\(n\) <= c1c2 f\(n\)g\(n\).) Tj
T*
(Therefore d\(n\)e\(n\) = O\(f\(n\)g\(n\)\), using c = c1c2.) Tj
