(Question 2) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(example1: Theta\(n^2\). The inner loop executes j + 1 times for each) Tj
T*
(j from 0 through n - 1. The total is sum\(j + 1\) = n\(n + 1\)/2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(example2: Theta\(n\). Its one loop has n iterations, and each iteration) Tj
T*
(does a constant number of operations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(example3: Theta\(log n\). After t iterations, i = 2^t. The loop stops) Tj
T*
(when 2^t >= n^2, so t = ceil\(log2\(n^2\)\) = Theta\(log n\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(example4: Theta\(n\). The outer loop uses i values n, floor\(n/2\),) Tj
T*
(floor\(n/4\), and so on. The total inner-loop work is bounded above by) Tj
T*
(n + n/2 + n/4 + ... < 2n and is at least n from the first iteration.) Tj
T*
(It is therefore Theta\(n\).) Tj
